--
-- User-confirmed working: v6.0.1 (bills+tips), v6.1.0 (dishes), v6.2.0 (orders),
-- v6.3.0 (seating). This build adds ONE thing: auto serve. Nothing else changes.
--
-- User-captured serve traffic (2026-10-27). Two stages:
--
--  STAGE 1 - pick up from the kitchen (ONE Interacted call):
--    Events.Restaurant.Interactions.Interacted:FireServer(tycoon, {
--      HoldDuration=0.25, Id="140", ActionText="Serve",
--      WorldPosition=Vector3.new(1208.80,0.27,316.02),
--      GamepadKeyCode=Enum.KeyCode.Thumbstick2, TemporaryPart=workspace.Temp.Part,
--      KeyboardKeyCode=Enum.KeyCode.F, Range=9, IsCustomerPrompt=true, Key="Serve",
--      Model=Items.Surface.K16, Part=workspace.Temp.Part, Prompt=workspace.Temp.Part["140"],
--      InteractionType="OrderCounter" })
--  STAGE 2 - hand each dish to the guest who ordered it (ONE TaskCompleted per dish):
--    TaskCompleted:FireServer({FoodModel=Objects.Food["10"], Name="Serve",
--                              Tycoon=tycoon, GroupId="19", CustomerId="2"})
--    ...and the same shape for Food["7"]->17/2 and Food["1"]->16/2.
--
-- IMPORTANT: each Serve call carries BOTH the dish and the guest ids together. The dish does
-- not know who ordered it (confirmed earlier: a dish has only EatMethod/Taken/Part:Head/
-- TestNewPlate/Contents). So the script pairs them by trying guests in turn - the server
-- accepts only the dish that guest actually ordered, which is how the three captured pairs
-- differ per dish.
--
-- INFERENCES (not in the capture, stated plainly):
--   * the counter is found as an Items.Surface child whose name does NOT match ^T%d+$
--     (tables are T1/T19; the capture shows K16 for the counter). If none is found, stage 1
--     is skipped and only stage 2 runs.
--   * `ProximityPromptStyle` is omitted - it is an enum value that cannot be reproduced.
--   * `Prompt` is whatever object exists at workspace.Temp named as in the capture, else the
--     part itself.
--
-- SPEED: seating 3-5 s delay was reported. Loop already ticks 0.2 s; SeatEvery is now 0.3 and
-- the per-group seat cooldown stays 10 s so a walking group is not re-seated. The remaining
-- delay is most likely the group appearing in ClientCustomers after it spawns - game-side.
--
-- Crash hardening unchanged: token bucket 8 calls / 0.5 s (do NOT raise), one target per
-- feature per pass, ClassName-only part lookup, no task.wait inside collection.
-- Upgrades excluded. No Instance.new.
-- Loader:
-- loadstring(game:HttpGet("https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bobashid/roblox-matcha/refs/heads/main/Restaurant%20Tycoon%203?v=" .. tostring(os.time()), true))()

